  "methodology": "Choose the cheapest tested configuration of each workflow that meets each minimum OBSERVED exact-accuracy floor. Both workflows may select any recorded prompt, including lower-accuracy configurations. Use complete selected passes, equal 300-turn counts and each recorded explicit price schedule. Report total input+output tokens separately from price-weighted estimated cost. Historical execution times and code versions differ. Selection uses known development results; there is no new independent validation, interpolation or claim that this is the optimal frontier over untested configurations.",
  "limitations": [
    "100 unique annotated turns repeated three times; observations are correlated and do not establish population accuracy.",
    "At 300 scored predictions, accuracy changes in 1/300 steps (about 0.33 percentage points); a 99.5% observed floor permits one error. This does not validate true 99.5% accuracy.",
    "The available full-history prompts are a limited search. A future sweep must optimize both workflows and evaluate selected configurations on independent conversations.",
    "Workflow costs exclude discarded/failed execution overhead, as in source summaries; all sources preserve separate accounting.",
    "Original versus follow-up runs include the previously documented parser fix; comparisons are historical development references."
